    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.46) anchor our lineup as the premier starts. **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Bieber (5.48 xERA), with the projection rewarding his dynamic platoon advantage and current high-efficiency status. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is a priority play; the favorable park factor and the opportunity to hit in the two-hole against a vulnerable starter make him a foundational piece for our Roto points today. We are also monitoring the speed-focused profile of **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65), whose score is elevated by the 100th percentile SB environment against Quantrill, making him an essential start given our desperate need to gain ground in stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the marginal tier at middle infield and utility. **Masyn Winn** (41.61) narrowly made the cut, but his floor remains precarious due to the relative difficulty of the matchup against Schlittler (2.85 xERA). He only barely outperformed the bench options like **Zack Gelof** or **Wenceel Perez**, primarily because we need to maintain our daily game cap efficiency; if the official lineups reflect any further defensive shifts or lineup drops for **Masyn Winn**, we will not hesitate to pull the plug to preserve our cap. **Kyle Karros** (55.40) provides a better stability profile today, as the combination of his elevated position in the order and the favorable platoon profile against the pitcher's slow delivery creates a legitimate opportunity for a stolen base.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the bottom third of our lineup. **Yainer Diaz** (56.58) draws a green light due to the pitching matchup, but his slot at number eight is a drag on his raw projection. We are currently operating with **Will Smith** on the IL and several key bats like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Lawrence Butler** sidelined by team off-days, which limits our ability to rotate in high-upside alternatives like **Matt Chapman** or **JJ Bleday**. Ensure you are monitoring the weather in the Cleveland and St. Louis matchups; any late-breaking rain delay could force us to pivot toward our reserves to avoid a zero-point day in the utility spot currently held by **Bryce Harper**.",
